WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.060
[Music]

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:11.280
The past holds within it a trove of stories&nbsp;
that continue to shape the present and future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:18.480
one such story is out of Andrew Jackson the&nbsp;
seventh president of the United States who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:24.420
fatally wounded a man during a duel in the&nbsp;
early 1800s and instead of getting condemned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.280
and thrown in jail for it he received praise&nbsp;
and recognition that helped him attain the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:37.020
highest political position in the country in a&nbsp;
time where personal honor was a prized virtue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:42.180
Mr Jackson took the risk of taking another&nbsp;
man's life for the sake of his reputation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:48.060
Jackson's opponent was a man named Charles&nbsp;
Dickinson, a hot-headed and quarrelsome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:53.400
lawyer residing in the state of Tennessee he was&nbsp;
known for being a skilled Marksman and a duelist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.400 --> 00:01:00.060
and was involved in at least 26 duels during&nbsp;
his lifetime the animosity between Jackson and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:06.600
Dickinson had been building for years fueled by&nbsp;
insults, accusations and even a horse race that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:13.200
ended in controversy one of the first disputes&nbsp;
happened in 1803 when Jackson served as a judge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:19.140
in a case involving a debt owed by Dickinson to&nbsp;
a man named George Eliot Dickinson had borrowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.780
money from Elliot and had not paid it back and&nbsp;
Elliot sued him to recover it as the judge in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:30.840
the matter Jackson ruled in favor of Elliot&nbsp;
Dickinson was enraged by this decision however&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:37.380
and challenged Jackson to a duel in response&nbsp;
Jackson accepted the challenge but the two men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:42.780
were prevented from fighting at the time due to&nbsp;
the intervention of local authorities the incident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:48.720
only served to increase the tension between the&nbsp;
two men and set the stage for later confrontations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:56.400
in 1805 at a horse race in Nashville Tennessee&nbsp;
Jackson entered his prized Thoroughbred into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:02.640
the race and bet a significant amount of money on&nbsp;
him to win Dickinson who was known for his skills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.940
as a horseman and gambler also entered a horse to&nbsp;
compete during the race their horses were neck and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:14.880
neck with Jackson shouting encouragement to his&nbsp;
horse as they approached the Finish Line in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:22.440
end Jackson's Thoroughbred won by a slim margin&nbsp;
According to some witnesses Dickinson was enraged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:27.840
by this outcome and accused Jackson of cheating,&nbsp;
claiming that by wearing weighted stirrups,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:33.840
Jackson's horse had an unfair Advantage the&nbsp;
argument between the two men became heated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:41.760
and at one point, Dickinson insulted Jackson's&nbsp;
wife Rachel later that same year, Dickinson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.040
published a letter in a local newspaper accusing&nbsp;
Jackson of cheating and of having a violent temper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.660
he also again made insulting remarks about&nbsp;
Jackson's wife Rachel finally the line had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.660 --> 00:03:00.900
been crossed with Jackson, and he officially&nbsp;
challenged his rival to a duel to defend his honor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:08.940
and thus, on May 30th 1806, the two men met&nbsp;
on the banks of the Red River in Logan County&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:15.180
Kentucky the exact number of people who attended&nbsp;
the duel is not known, but it's estimated that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:21.720
between 30 and 100 people may have been present to&nbsp;
witness the event that day according to witnesses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:26.640
the weather was hot and humid with the sun&nbsp;
beating down on the two men as they stood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:32.700
facing each other the atmosphere surrounding&nbsp;
the duel was tense and charged with emotion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:40.140
both men were known for their fiery personalities&nbsp;
and quick tempers, and the insults and accusations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:47.160
that had led to the challenge had only served to&nbsp;
intensify the animosity between them despite the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:52.560
gravity of the situation, the rules of the duel&nbsp;
were followed with strict adherence to protocol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:59.700
and these rules were simple, 24 feet apart,&nbsp;
each man with the pistol and the first to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:04.740
hit his opponent would be declared the winner&nbsp;
after each man's assistants, called seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:11.820
carefully measured out the distance between the&nbsp;
two combatants, the two men stood silently glaring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:18.900
at each other in the Kentucky sunlight and the&nbsp;
duel began Jackson took aim, but hesitated before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:25.140
firing Dickinson, however, did not hesitate and&nbsp;
fired his shot, hitting Jackson in the chest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:30.600
and fracturing his arm Jackson Managed to cover&nbsp;
the wound with his hand to contain the bleeding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:36.660
and while remaining calm and upright, he aimed&nbsp;
and fired, striking Dickinson in the chest and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:43.080
fatally wounding him while Dickinson's assistants&nbsp;
contended that Jackson's first shot had misfired,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:47.640
which would have signaled the end of The&nbsp;
Duel, Jackson had disregarded this tradition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:54.900
by resetting his gun and firing again, ultimately&nbsp;
causing Dickinson's fatality though Jackson would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.900 --> 00:05:00.600
eventually recover from his own wound, the injury&nbsp;
left him with persistent discomfort throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:07.080
remainder of his life not long afterward Jackson&nbsp;
was charged with murder by the authorities in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:12.780
Kentucky but he was eventually acquitted the&nbsp;
incident caused a great deal of controversy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:19.200
was heavily criticized by some who viewed dueling&nbsp;
as barbaric and archaic despite the criticism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:24.660
Jackson's reputation as a man of honor and&nbsp;
integrity only grew following the event&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:30.960
he would go on to serve in numerous political&nbsp;
positions afterward, even as the seventh president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:36.660
of the United States and so the famous duel&nbsp;
between Andrew Jackson and Charles Dickinson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:41.880
was cemented in history a tragic event&nbsp;
that highlights the importance placed on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:48.360
personal honor and reputation in the past while&nbsp;
dueling may seem barbaric and unnecessary today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:54.840
it was a commonly accepted practice in the&nbsp;
19th century Jackson's methods in the duel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.840 --> 00:06:01.320
helped to solidify his reputation as a man of&nbsp;
great integrity and courage, a reputation that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:06.780
would follow him throughout his life and career&nbsp;
The Duel can also be seen as a pivotal moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:12.480
in American history, a dramatic clash between&nbsp;
two formidable men that spoke to the tensions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:18.300
and rivalries of the era while the outcome of&nbsp;
the duel is a matter of record, with Jackson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:24.960
emerging Victorious but badly wounded, the deeper&nbsp;
significance of the event lies in what it revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:30.300
about the character of the men involved and the&nbsp;
broader societal forces that shaped their lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:37.560
for Jackson The Duel was a test of his honor and&nbsp;
reputation, a chance to defend his wife's honor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:43.260
and establish himself as a man of courage and&nbsp;
conviction for Dickinson, it was an opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:49.680
to prove his own mettle and assert his dominance&nbsp;
over a rival yet in the end, both men were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:55.380
changed by the experience and the legacy of their&nbsp;
conflict would resonate for generations to come

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:08.760
thank you

